/**
 * @defgroup DspCore_Example_TransformsFourier Fourier transforms
 * @ingroup DspCore_Examples_Transforms
 * @brief Compare direct DFT and radix-2 FFT, then reconstruct with IFFT.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_TransformsFourier_Goal Goal
 * Configure a four-sample direct DFT and radix-2 FFT, transform an alternating
 * real signal, then invert the FFT result. Both forward transforms put the
 * signal at the Nyquist bin; Inverse applies the normalizing `1/N` factor.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_TransformsFourier_Run Run
 * @code{.bash}
 * ./build/macos_arm64/bin/Debug/DspCore_Transforms_Fourier_d
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_TransformsFourier_Output Output
 * @code{.text}
 * Nyquist bin: DFT=4, FFT=4; expected=4
 * FFT inverse first sample=1; expected=1
 * Overall: PASS
 * @endcode
 *
 * Configure performs the only allocation. ForwardReal, Forward and Inverse
 * use the configured workspace and therefore do not allocate. DFT accepts any
 * nonzero size; FFT requires a power of two.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_TransformsFourier_Code Implementation
 * \include Transforms/Fourier/Shared.cpp
 */
